8247699141502, 0.019217951223254204, 0.0046033700928092, -0.013369564898312092, 0.026151737198233604, 0.005216301418840885, 0.020188426598906517, -0.03516693785786629, -0.02202722057700157, -0.023508470505475998, -0.04584215581417084, -0.01883487030863762, -0.0070806341245770454, -0.021720753982663155, 0.011888314038515091, 0.04852373152971268, -0.01654914580285549, 0.032791826874017715]], "input": ["# Canadian Home Parenteral Nutrition Registry Community\n\nThe community is centered around the Canadian Home Parenteral Nutrition (HPN) Registry, which collects data on home parenteral nutrition in Canada. Key contributors include researchers Allard JP and Armstrong D, who play significant roles in the registry's operations and data collection efforts.\n\n## Significance of the Canadian HPN Registry\n\nThe Canadian HPN Registry is a crucial entity in this community, focusing on collecting data related to home parenteral nutrition in Canada. This registry aims to improve patient outcomes by validating practices and outcomes associated with home parenteral nutrition. The data collected can influence clinical practices and policies, making it a vital resource for healthcare providers and researchers alike. The registry's focus on patient outcomes underscores its importance in the healthcare landscape. [Data: Entities (16356), Relationships (19421)]\n\n## Contributions of Allard JP\n\nAllard JP is a key researcher contributing to the Canadian HPN Registry. His involvement signifies the importance of academic and clinical research in enhancing the quality of data collected. Allard's contributions may include research design, data analysis, and interpretation of findings, which are essential for the registry's credibility and effectiveness. His role highlights the collaborative nature of the community, where researchers work together to improve patient care through data-driven insights. [Data: Entities (16366), Relationships (20555)]\n\n## Role of Armstrong D in the registry